<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1661">1661</a>–<a href="/years/1706">1706</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville was a soldier and explorer born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>. He raided English posts on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a> and in 1696-1697 destroyed most English settlements on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> from Plaisance. In 1699 he built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-maurepas">Fort Maurepas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biloxi">Biloxi</a>, beginning the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville.jpg" alt="Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait,_Pierre_Le_Moyne_d%27Iberville,_Montr%C3%A9al_Archives.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Louisiana, founded by <b>Pierre Le Moyne d’Iberville</b> in 1699, had its own governor and became a separate colony, while the western posts were run by military commandants who relied on gift-giving and diplomacy with their Native allies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/new-france">New France · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Settlement began when <b>Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</b> built Fort Maurepas at Biloxi in 1699.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-louisiana">French Louisiana</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1696 to 1697 <b>Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</b> led raids from Plaisance that destroyed most English settlements on Newfoundland, including St John's.</blockquote><a href="/state/plaisance">Plaisance</a></li><li><blockquote>French raids under <b>Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</b> captured several posts until the Treaty of Utrecht in 1713.</blockquote><a href="/state/ruperts-land">Rupert's Land</a></li></ul></section>
